{
  "inShort": "The artifacts show preparation, so the playable goal is at risk. Four tasks closed, but none proves a playable jump or first level. The devlog claims a web build without linking it, and its media does not show the game.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hf200z5xoz8qjmdfvfi",
      "text": "A public repository of the Godot demo projects the game builds on is complete. The inspected repository contains demo folders and import instructions. It provides starting material, not evidence of this game running."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hff00z6xoz88svm5zwp",
      "text": "An animated reference video for the art style is complete. Its title and thumbnail show Big Buck Bunny, but the animation was not inspected. This supplies a visual reference, not a chosen style. The devlog also links this film and labels a mountain photograph as a jumping gnome. Neither verifies the reported jump."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hfy00z7xoz83i3lhw8g",
      "text": "A reference article on what playtesting is, for the team to read is complete. The inspected Wikipedia article explains playtesting and its types. It does not show that anyone tested this prototype."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmw2b6hgb00z8xoz82dr7tqni",
      "text": "A private design board for the team is complete through its attached artifact. Its contents were not inspected, so no conclusions about level design or the chosen style follow."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [
    "cmw2b6hgm00z9xoz8wh9h1eua"
  ],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Where can anyone open the reported web build and test the jump and first level?",
    "What uncertainty about the playable goal would A storyboard for the trailer resolve?"
  ],
  "direction": {
    "goal": {
      "value": "toward",
      "why": "The public Godot demo repository supplies starting material for the playable build, though the jump and level remain unverified."
    },
    "stage": {
      "value": "toward",
      "why": "The art reference adds visible material for choosing a style, but neither a chosen style nor a working core was demonstrated."
    }
  },
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "“Devlog #1” announces an itch.io build without a playable link and received 0 applause and 0 views; no game page is listed.",
    "team": "Alex’s stated hours leave about 30–45 hours, with Mia’s capacity uncounted. Both joined and confirmed work, giving the prototype active programming coverage, but one sprint cannot establish pace.",
    "management": "Four tasks closed, yet the remaining trailer storyboard cannot by itself deliver the jump or level. With 30–45 stated hours left, keep the storyboard secondary and put the playable build and first level into the tasks."
  }
}

